comments[9]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T04:50:19.034Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "created_at=now,text=Duplicate check: complete3034-item all-status snapshot plus complete seven-hit session suppressed row types search and refreshed open/in-progress inventories found no exact active leaf. Live full pm-hid9g1 confirms session suppression is completed and preserved, while pm-oybmsd is limited to producer metadata envelopes. Source evidence: applyReadOutputSessionReferences and the existing read-output-contracts session replacement regression. This follow-up remains open/unclaimed and is not part of the two active implementations."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T07:15:47.123Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Implementation start: model session reference rows at declared collection paths, preserve ordinary non-session result types, and prove source plus packed declaration consumers. Connected delivery also addresses GH1528 same-command read-option recovery; unrelated backlog remains open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T07:19:58.060Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Regression sensitivity: unchanged declarations failed seven assertions in tests/types/read-session-results.test-d.ts, including unused expected-error directives for context prose, nested search item access and declared object-map rows. The same consumer also exposed context_ref as unknown. Implementing a typed session-result transform and public structural narrowing guard; budget-only/no-session calls retain original row shapes."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T07:42:25.663Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Expanded package-author acceptance in an isolated checkout: literal nested maps, dynamic row-key arrays, optional row contracts, overlapping parent/child row declarations and item_id identities now admit session references without weakening ordinary no-session types. Source compile consumers pass. Full static run passed code quality, SDK boundaries, contract/recovery/token checks, then correctly stopped on missing expected_result for the new recovery leaf; corrected through pm update and linked both defects to existing recurrence families."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T09:23:12.011Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Full local coverage attempt on Homebrew Node26.9.0:10941 tests passed,3 skipped and1 packed-consumer fixture failed before packing because npm/package.json is outside that runtime standard lookup roots. No coverage summary was emitted after the test failure, so this is not a coverage pass. Re-running unchanged source on installed Node24.21.0, matching hosted CI and exposing its bundled npm normally. Public registry verifier and separate npm/Bun installed-agent acceptance remain successful."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T09:30:37.370Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final focused acceptance: linked typecheck and real npm-tarball declaration consumers pass with the advertised npm lookup environment, including literal/dynamic/optional/overlapping/numeric row paths. Both Node and Bun packed runtime matrices pass19 scenarios and conflict guards. The earlier host npm-discovery failure remains in test history. GitHub intake:23 open issues all carry PM-link comments; no open PRs or dependency/code/secret alerts; audit has0 vulnerabilities. Current release2026.10.21 and both installed-manager journeys pass. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with0 high/critical,2.38percent error rate and0 missing-code rows; recent matched start/finish sessions and physical queue0 were independently read. Pending compatible updates remain under existing cooldown/migration owners."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T09:35:16.655Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Changelog checkpoint: npm now publishes pm-changelog2026.10.21, consumed by the canonical install/generate/check scripts. Package-owned output adds the two new Fixed entries and reclassifies historical duplicate/already-fixed/not-reproducible closures; sampled live terminal metadata supports those changes. No generator was patched or hand-edited in pm-cli. Terminal defect evidence, validation and health pass after closure; current in-progress population was empty at that checkpoint."
    edited_at: "2026-10-21T10:05:33.643Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T11:10:16.440Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CodeRabbit thread4335926304 confirmed a direct-helper typing regression. New session-free helper consumer cases fail on the pre-fix declarations with missing item/title diagnostics. The helper now infers session capability from camel/snake options, keeps budget omissions, distributes option unions and retains existing explicit Result type arguments. Optional, dynamic and session-bearing cases still require reference narrowing. Full source typecheck passes; the generated SDK snapshot records3 acknowledged signature changes. Packed declaration acceptance is next."
  - created_at: "2026-10-21T11:15:00.723Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Final review remediation passes source typecheck and the real packed declaration consumer with the precise helper cases. The same linked run passes all19 runtime continuation scenarios on Node and Bun. Ordinary and budget-only helper rows retain prose, while optional, union, dynamic and snake-case session options require narrowing. Lint and SDK snapshot checks pass with the3 conservative signature acknowledgements. Previous-head repository coverage is100/100/100/100; the revised head must independently pass the unchanged hosted checks."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T09:30:39.202Z","harness:codex","Session result declarations must follow runtime row identities and paths: nested search hits, item_id, optional or dynamic contracts, overlapping declarations and numeric array segments all admit fact references. Preserve precise ordinary reads and provide a structural guard for schema-extensible rows."
  "2026-10-21T11:10:18.097Z","harness:codex","Session capability must be inferred at every public result-producing boundary, including direct shaping helpers. Keep no-session options precise while admitting references for optional, aliased, union and dynamically typed session values; validate the same consumer through source and real packed declarations."
